## 5. Preliminary Technical Assessment

The intermittent nature of the reported problem indicates that actuator behavior is not consistent under the described operating conditions.

Successful operation during some cycles does not establish that the pneumatic supply, directional-control valve, actuator, sensors, or control system function correctly during abnormal cycles.

The reported association with increased production activity warrants further investigation, but no verified evidence establishes a causal relationship.

Changes in the local pressure indication cannot be reliably interpreted without knowing the measurement location, instrument condition, and operating circumstances.

The reported failure of the automated sequence may involve actual actuator movement, control commands, feedback behavior, or another unverified condition.

**Current technical conclusion:** No failed component or root cause has been established.

